      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]=$",
      "worked_solution": "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2+0+0 & 1+0+0 & 4+0+0 \\\\ -4+0+2 & -2+15+2 & -8+0+4 \\\\ 0+0+2 & 0+5+2 & 0+0+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 15 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
